  'copilotAdoption.page.kpi.timeSaved.what': 'The time Microsoft 365 Copilot and Cowork could give back each month with full use, as a range. MODELLED, not measured, in two layers: Copilot\u2019s, from observed meetings, emails and documents, and Cowork\u2019s on top, from Cowork tasks - which no study has yet measured.',
  'copilotAdoption.page.kpi.timeSaved.how': 'The same model and assumptions as the Cowork tab - the product defaults, or the figures you entered there this session. The Cowork tab shows the evidence behind every Copilot assumption, checks Copilot\u2019s layer against published studies, and says plainly that Cowork\u2019s rests on an assumption.',
  'copilotAdoption.page.kpi.timeSaved.formula': 'Copilot hours = (meetings \u00d7 {meeting} + emails \u00d7 {email} + documents \u00d7 {document}) \u00f7 60; Cowork hours = (tasks observed + people not yet observed \u00d7 {rate}) \u00d7 {taskMinutes} \u00f7 60; conservative end = each \u00d7 {percent}%',
  'copilotAdoption.page.kpi.timeSaved.source': 'Volumes from Microsoft 365 usage reports and Microsoft\u2019s Cowork usage report. Not a measurement of time saved, and never a money figure.',


  'copilotAdoption.page.coworkEligibilityControlledSpendingPolicyScopeDeprecatedCoworkAgent': 'Cowork eligibility is controlled by spending-policy scope, not by the deprecated Cowork agent entry or by the Microsoft 365 Copilot licence count.',
