  'copilotAdoption.server.action.reclaim.description': 'Two routes reach this group, and both are safe to act on. A disabled account still holding a seat is the clearest reclaim there is whatever its usage looked like before it was disabled - no enablement effort is worthwhile on an account nobody can sign into. The rest had no Copilot activity anywhere in the last {historyDays} days - the whole history this analysis reads - and have enough account tenure to judge: confirm the licence is still needed before renewal. New starters inside the grace period and users with no tenure evidence are NOT here; they are under \'Review before reclaim\'.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.reengage.description': 'Used Copilot before this period but not once inside it. Someone who tried it and stopped is a different problem from someone who never started - ask what stopped and offer a refresher. These seats carry the review-only reclaim tier, so confirm with the user or their manager before reassigning one: leave, part-time patterns and role changes are not visible in usage data.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.coach.description': 'Occasional use only (engagement below {developingScore}). The cheapest move is one repeatable habit in the app they already live in, rather than a general Copilot training session.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.broaden.description': 'Real, regular use - but almost entirely in a single Copilot surface. Introducing one more surface (Outlook summaries, Teams meeting recaps) is the cheapest remaining gain for these users, because they have already accepted Copilot and simply have not been shown where else it works.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.grow.description': 'Engagement between {developingScore} and {establishedScore} across more than one surface. A short scenario-based session aimed at their actual job is what moves this group to daily use.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.sustain.description': 'Engagement at or above {establishedScore} across multiple surfaces - Copilot is part of their working week. No action needed; these are the licences that are paying for themselves.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.advocate.description': 'Engagement at or above {championScore} - among your deepest users. Ask them to run a peer session for their own department, which converts better than centrally run training. If their breadth score is low they are still worth showing one more surface.',
  'copilotAdoption.server.action.review.description': 'Potential reclaim cases that are too new to judge, or missing enough tenure or account-state context to act on automatically. Leave, part-time patterns, service accounts and shared mailboxes are not detectable from usage data, so a human review is required. Dormant seats are deliberately NOT here - they get the Win back action, because there is still somebody to talk to - but they are counted as review-only in the reclaim tiers, which is a seat decision rather than an enablement one.',
